# LANE DECISION — depends on the probe result (fill in when writing Commit 2)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cron.py already SKIPS (never fails) any lane whose config/approval is absent; Commit 2
# must NOT weaken those skip-not-fail gates. What the probe decides:
#
#   * If NSE `browser=` codes are 200 from the runner:
#       The NSE-touching lanes (NSE discovery, NSE identity/ISIN/listing-date backfill,
#       NSE per-IPO lifecycle) may run on Actions. No extra gating needed.
#
#   * If NSE `browser=` codes are 403 from the runner IPs:
#       The NSE-touching lanes must be GATED OFF in this workflow and documented as
#       owner-PC-only. Pass `--skip-*`-style flags or an env gate so those lanes report
#       "skipped: owner-PC-only (NSE 403 from runner IPs)" rather than failing — the DB,
#       R2/SBI, Kite (validate-only), snapshot-publish, and scoring lanes still run on
#       Actions. (cron.py has --skip-download / --skip-rhp-download / --skip-kite today;
#       a discovery/identity/lifecycle skip switch may need to be added — decide with the
#       owner based on the dry-run output, without weakening the existing gates.)
#
# RULES CARRIED INTO COMMIT 2: no secret values in code or logs (names/codes only);
# every secret read as ${{ secrets.NAME }}; do not weaken cron.py's skip-not-fail gates;
# full local gate before push.